'''''Oxalis exilis''''', the '''least yellow sorrel''' or '''shady woodsorrel''',<ref>{{Cite web |title=Oxalis exilis - Cunn. |url=https://pfaf.org/user/Plant.aspx?LatinName=Oxalis+exilis |access-date=14 February 2023 |website=[[Plants For a Future]]}}</ref> is a small [[herbaceous plant]] found in Australia and New Zealand.{{r|plantnet|wa|edible}} It is mainly found in hillsides and weedy areas. It is the smallest species of ''[[Oxalis]]'' in New Zealand.{{r|sykes2009}} The colors of the leaves range from green to purple. The capsule and style length vary from 4–6.5 mm.{{r|sykes2009}}

